<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Ribe</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Ribe is a town in south-west <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jutland">Jutland</a>, regarded as the oldest town in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/denmark">Denmark</a>. It began as a trading place in the early eighth century, linked to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/frisia">Frisia</a> and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/north-sea">North Sea</a> trade, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ansgar">Ansgar</a> built one of the first churches in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/scandinavia">Scandinavia</a> there around 860. It became a bishopric, and its Romanesque cathedral dates from the twelfth century. It declined after the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/ribe.jpg" alt="Ribe" width="320" height="180" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Hjart · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:RibeVue.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
